# =============================================================================
# Node Version Manager (nvm) Configuration
# =============================================================================
#
# Specifies the Node.js version for this project.
# Documentation: https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm
#
# This file is portable - copy to other repos without modification.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How It Works
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# When you `cd` into a directory with .nvmrc, nvm can automatically switch
# to the specified Node.js version (if configured with auto-use).
#
# This ensures all developers use the same Node.js version, preventing
# "works on my machine" issues caused by version differences.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Usage
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   Install the specified version:
#     nvm install
#
#   Switch to the specified version:
#     nvm use
#
#   Set as default:
#     nvm alias default $(cat .nvmrc)
#
#   Check current version:
#     node --version
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auto-Use Configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Add to ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc for automatic version switching:
#
#   # Automatically call `nvm use` when entering directory with .nvmrc
#   autoload -U add-zsh-hook
#   load-nvmrc() {
#     local nvmrc_path="$(nvm_find_nvmrc)"
#     if [ -n "$nvmrc_path" ]; then
#       local nvmrc_node_version=$(nvm version "$(cat "${nvmrc_path}")")
#       if [ "$nvmrc_node_version" = "N/A" ]; then
#         nvm install
#       elif [ "$nvmrc_node_version" != "$(nvm version)" ]; then
#         nvm use
#       fi
#     fi
#   }
#   add-zsh-hook chpwd load-nvmrc
#   load-nvmrc
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supported Formats
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   22          Major version (latest 22.x.x)
#   22.11       Minor version (latest 22.11.x)
#   22.11.0     Exact version
#   lts/*       Latest LTS release
#   lts/iron    Specific LTS codename (Node 20)
#   lts/jod     Specific LTS codename (Node 22)
#   node        Latest current release
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node.js 22 LTS Features
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Pinned to an exact 22.x: the lockfiles' engines need >=22.22.2, and a bare
# `22` lets nvm pick any older 22.x that is already installed.
#
# Node.js 22 (codename "Jod") became LTS in October 2024.
# Key features:
#   - V8 JavaScript engine 12.4
#   - Stable ES modules
#   - Native fetch() API
#   - Built-in test runner
#   - WebSocket client
#   - Better ESM/CJS interoperability
#
# =============================================================================
22.22.2
